{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 35, :comments ["<b>הן תוי</b> — Some say: it is deficient [of an] alef, and the meaning is \"I longed that Shaddai answer me.\" The correct interpretation: it is like והתוית תי\"ו (Ezek. 9:4, \"and you marked a tav\"), and the meaning is, all that I have written — Shaddai is the One who will answer me." "<b>איש ריבי</b> — Who would plead on my behalf."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {0 "Resolved the quotation of Ezekiel 9:4 by inserting the verse reference for clarity, since Ibn Ezra quotes only the Hebrew words without citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:12.438258691Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}